  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Improving Access to COVID-19 Vaccination for Vulnerable Migrants and Mobile Populations in Humanitarian Settings in Afghanistan</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Afghanistan continues to report a significant number of COVID-19 cases. Despite efforts by multiple partners to increase the availability of the COVID-19 vaccine since February 2021 to November 2022, the proportion of the population that is fully vaccinated remains low. While vaccination efforts are underway, numerous barriers such as those related to public policies, and multiple other access-related issues including language and affordability continue to exist. These barriers are heightened for particularly for vulnerable and harder to reach groups, such as migrants, internally displaced persons (IDPs), refugees, rural and remote populations and, increasingly, women and girls who often already struggle to access healthcare services in the areas where they reside. In line with the 2023 National Deployment and Vaccination Plan, priorities to increase overall coverage and ultimately contribute to &#x201c;leaving no one behind&#x201d; with regards to COVID-19 vaccines in Afghanistan, the project will contribute to strengthening and accelerating COVID-19 vaccination as well as routine immunization among vulnerable migrants and mobile populations including returnees, IDPs in five main border provinces with the highest number of undocumented migrants returning from Pakistan and Iran.</narrative>
  </description>
